      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='16'>Title:</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='16'> What specific transaction behavior perfectly isolates awakened mule accounts from legitimate users?</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Subtitle:</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'> Awakened mules exhibit an immediate &quot;emptying&quot; pattern, transferring out &gt;95% of incoming funds, establishing a near-perfect positive correlation with fraudulent activity.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
      </layout-options>
      <table>
